cl names an unnamed namespace `?A0x<hash>@`, and the hash is not a fact about the language: it is derived from the translation unit, so cl's answer for this file and clang-cl's `?A0x372253CB` are different names for the same namespace, and neither is more right. There is nothing here for two compilers to agree on. cxx1 writes `_GLOBAL__N_1`, which the Itanium ABI does specify - and on both Itanium targets this case agrees with clang exactly, name for name. What can be checked on this target is checked: the case is in run-cases.cmd and passes, so the linkage is right even though the spelling of the namespace is arbitrary. See tests/cases/namespace-unnamed.nonames for the same difference against clang-cl.
